# Build artifacts
sim/build/
sim/datacenter/htsim_uec
sim/datacenter/htsim_*.o
sim/parse_output

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Local sweep ephemerals (regenerated on each run)
**/experiments/runs/*/sweep.pid
**/experiments/runs/*/jobs_light.txt
**/experiments/runs/*/jobs_heavy.txt
**/experiments/runs/*/work/

# Very large regenerable matrices (regen via gen_all_matrices.sh)
**/experiments/runs/*/matrices/allreduce_ring_1024n_*.cm
**/experiments/runs/*/matrices/allreduce_butterfly_*.cm

# htsim's default logfile if a run ever writes it in-tree
sim/datacenter/logout.dat
sim/datacenter/idmap.txt

# ============================================================================
# Added 2026-09-21, after `git add .` swept 1,556 MB into a commit. The rules
# above were written for the workloads that existed then; the rail study and
# fidelityRuns introduced patterns nothing covered.
# ============================================================================

# Per-run htsim logs: one line per finished flow, so a 536k-flow run produces a
# ~125 MB file and the set totals ~1.3 GB. GitHub REJECTS any file over 100 MB,
# so these cannot be pushed even if you wanted them. They are reproduced by
# re-running, and the .row/.urow next to them hold the actual extracted results.
**/experiments/runs/**/logs/*.log

# Large regenerable connection matrices (218 MB). gen_rail_aware_allreduce.py and
# gen_rail_aware_alltoall.py are deterministic and reproduce these BYTE-FOR-BYTE
# (verified with cmp), so there is no reason to put them in history.
# Regenerate with: fidelityRuns/bin/regen_matrices.sh
**/experiments/runs/*/matrices/rail_*.cm

# fidelityRuns stages COPIES of matrices that are either tracked at their original
# location or regenerable. Never commit the copies.
**/experiments/runs/fidelityRuns/matrices/

# Sweep progress logs: scheduling noise, not data. Which runs finished, and with
# what numbers, is recorded in the results CSVs next to them.
**/experiments/runs/*/*.progress.log

# fidelityRuns run-time ephemerals
**/experiments/runs/fidelityRuns/work/
**/experiments/runs/fidelityRuns/sweep_*
**/experiments/runs/fidelityRuns/*.tar.gz

# ...but these ARE deliverables, and the ROOT .gitignore's `*.csv` / `*.png`
# would otherwise swallow them. A deeper .gitignore overrides a shallower one.
!**/experiments/runs/fidelityRuns/MANIFEST.csv
!**/experiments/runs/fidelityRuns/results/*.csv
!**/experiments/runs/fidelityRuns/graphs/*.png

# The packaged result set is a deliverable too: 197 KB holding all 1305 .row +
# 1305 .urow, so the analysis can be run from a single download instead of a
# 2610-file clone. `tar czf` here is byte-reproducible from identical input
# (verified by md5), so re-packaging unchanged data adds no new blob.
!**/experiments/runs/fidelityRuns/fidelity_results.tar.gz

# stray wget output
sim/wget-log

# The project report is a 1.5 MB binary: it does not diff, so every revision would
# store a whole new copy in history.
HTSIM_Project_Report.docx
**/HTSIM_Project_Report.docx

# Local backups taken while patching the harness mid-sweep (2026-09-28). Every
# patched file is tracked, so git history already holds each previous version --
# these copies exist only for quick local revert and must not enter the repo.
**/experiments/runs/fidelityRuns/**/*.orig
**/experiments/runs/fidelityRuns/**/*.bak-*
**/experiments/runs/fidelityRuns/MANIFEST.csv.pre-*

# Guard runtime log: operational noise, same category as *.progress.log above.
# What ran and with what result is in the .row files and the results CSVs.
**/experiments/runs/fidelityRuns/oom_guard.log
